  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1203.51 Multi-component coating",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1203.51 “Multi-component coating” means a coating requiring the addition, before application, of a separate reactive resin, commonly known as a catalyst or hardener, in order to form an acceptable dry film.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
